-- title:
--   Asymptotic power bound for the complete band-prime arithmetic budget
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural exponent $k$. Let $T_k(n)$ be the explicit band-prime time budget: prime-pool construction plus the product of the prime-chain depth allowance, candidate-band count, squared pool-size allowance, and per-triple arithmetic budget, with its factor $15$. Let $E=128H_2(1/256)$, where $H_2$ is binary entropy, and use the fixed parameters $\varepsilon=1/5$ and $\sigma=-1/20$.
--
--   For every real $\eta>0$, all sufficiently large natural $n$ satisfy
--   $$T_k(n)\le n^{\,2+\varepsilon(4/5-(2/5)E-2\sigma)+\eta}.$$
--   The threshold may depend on $k$ and $\eta$.
--
--   This bounds all executed arithmetic in the band-prime stage at its stated exponent, while allowing arbitrarily small asymptotic slack.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/BandPrimeCostBounds.lean#L54-L69

